{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"37a9f2d2a1fced82c495f07275d7b9ba377c12b03df1f3ce4fca3ed0eb1ced09","digest":{"component_or_area":"Backend port / reconciler transport abstraction","key_entities":["BackendHTTPError","_backend.py","dispatch_apply_phases.py","outbound_differ.py","jira_datacenter/transport.py","jira.exceptions.JIRAError","urllib.error.HTTPError","_safe_get_issue","_update_one_apply_reporter","_with_connection_retry"],"problem_keywords":["exception contract","transport abstraction","vendor-neutral core","exception translation","DC vs Cloud compatibility"],"propositions":["DC transport raises JIRAError which does not match the urllib.error.HTTPError catch clauses in dispatch_apply_phases.py and outbound_differ.py, causing exceptions to escape instead of degrading gracefully","outbound_differ._safe_get_issue cannot classify DC 404 errors as _DELETED because it only catches urllib.error.HTTPError, breaking deletion detection on DC","the core modules contain vendor-specific urllib.error.HTTPError imports, violating the principle that core should be transport-neutral","BackendHTTPError must be declared as a port contract subclassing urllib.error.HTTPError so existing catch clauses work without modification and .code attribute is preserved","the DC transport must translate JIRAError to BackendHTTPError at the adapter boundary, preserving the HTTP status code"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787520754554691001,"uuid":"7e2e7ace-59eb-477d-931e-ae566f8a02f2"}